# The root .gitignore's "[Bb]uild*/" rule (meant for CMake build output dirs) also matches any
# source directory named "builder". Re-include ours; this is tracked source code.
#
# Un-excluding the DIRECTORY is what makes this work: git will not re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so a rule naming the files alone would silently do nothing -- and the
# headers would go missing from the commit with no warning at all.
!src/builder
!dev_api/openvino/frontend/gguf/builder
